  "id": "Compound::DB00514 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Dextromethorphan appears to interact with Cyp2c19 through a series of interconnected metabolic and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Dextromethorphan binds to Cyp2b6, which then participates in the metabolism of arachidonic acid, a key step in the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. This pathway is also engaged by Cyp2e1, further reinforcing the involvement of Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1 in the same metabolic process. The shared participation of these cytochrome P450 enzymes in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity leads to their involvement in the metabolic pathway that ultimately involves Cyp2c19. This suggests a potential mechanism where Dextromethorphan indirectly influences Cyp2c19 through the activation of Cyp2b6 and Cyp2e1, which are both part of the same metabolic network. The evidence supports a dependency on these enzymes for the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid, and thus, the involvement of Cyp2c19 in this process.",
